===Adjective===
{{en-adj|more,er}}

# Distinguished by a [[unique]], [[particular]], or [[unusual]] quality.
#: {{ux|en|a '''special''' episode of a television series}}
#: {{ux|en|her '''special''' blend of spices}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=w:George Carlin|chapter=PLEASE DON'T SAY THAT|title=w:When Will Jesus Bring the Pork Chops?|url=https://archive.org/details/sacredmountainof0000john/|location=[[New York]]|publisher=w:Hyperion Books|ISBN=1-4013-0821-X|OCLC=757869006|OL=24604921M|page=132|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/whenwilljesusbri00hype/page/132/| text=EVERY CHILD IS '''SPECIAL'''<br>An empty and meaningless sentiment. What about every adult? Isn't every adult '''special'''? And if not, then at what age does a person go from being '''special''' to being not-so-'''special'''? And if every adult is also '''special''', then that means all people are '''special''' and the idea has no meaning.}}
# Of particular value or interest; [[dear]]; [[beloved]].
#: {{ux|en|Everyone is '''special''' to someone.}}
#: {{ux|en|his '''special''' friend of many years, Bill}}
# {{lb|en|military}} Of or related to [[unconventional]] [[warfare]].
#: {{ux|en|'''special''' forces, '''special''' operations}}
# {{lb|en|law}} Appointed specifically to examine a single event or issue.
#: {{ux|en|For the few times the U.S. Supreme Court has to actually try a case, they will appoint a '''special''' master to do so.}}
#: {{ux|en|After the ''Watergate'' break in, a '''special''' prosecutor was appointed.}}
# Constituting or relating to a [[species]].
#: {{syn|en|specific}}
#: {{ux|en|Having seven dark spots is a '''special''' property unique to {{taxfmt|Coccinella septempunctata|species}}.}}
# {{lb|en|euphemistic|not comparable}} Of or related to [[disability|disabilities]], especially [[learning disability|learning]] or [[intellectual disability|intellectual disabilities]].
#: {{ux|en|[[special education|'''special''' education]], [[special needs|'''special''' needs]]}}
#: {{ux|en|He goes to a '''special''' school.}}
## {{lb|en|by extension|pejorative|often|offensive|comparable}} [[stupid|Stupid]], lacking [[intelligence]].
##: {{usex|en|What do you mean, you don't understand the sign?  What are you, '''special'''?}}
# {{lb|en|euphemistic|not comparable}}
## Of, being, or pertaining to [[sexual intercourse]] or the [[genitals]].
##: {{ux|en|The parents told the kids not to bother them during '''special''' time.}}
##: {{ux|en|The girl said the man had tried to touch her '''special''' place.}}
## Infused with a [[drug]], especially [[marijuana]]; being an [[edible]].
##* {{quote-book|en|date=2012-11-01|author=Klyde|title=How To Hide The Smell Of Weed|publisher=Lulu.com|isbn=9781622094080|page=9
|text=This book will help you to {{nb...}} • Cook with the confidence that the neighbors won't find out your brownies are ''''special'''' • Never again worry about getting caught growing because someone smelled your garden}}
##* {{quote-book|en|date=2020-03-19|author=I. D. Oro|title=Mexico Wall 130|publisher=I. D. Oro|page=136
|text=Then with the rest of the money I use it to pay for the building, maintenance, utilities, up keep, and the '''special''' brownies! In addition, I have bongs that the parishioners can use if they forget to bring their own bongs for smoking.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|date=2021-06-15|author=Laura Heffernan|title=Sweet Reality|publisher=Empress Books
|text=“Jen, when someone offers you ''''special'''' brownies or 'funny' brownies, they have pot in them. You're totally high right now.” Me, high? No way! No one ever offered the nerdy girl drugs. And I'd never, ever accept them.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|date=2021-09-23|author=Gillian A. Corsiatto|title=Duck Light|publisher=FriesenPress|isbn=9781039109629|page=5
|text=“They're '''special''' brownies,” said Rosie. Special brownies! Of course they were special! They were perfect and delicious! What a great word to describe them! Rosie caught on that Lulu had not caught on. “'''Special''' brownies. Happy brownies. {{nb...}} They're the ones that have weed in them.”}}

